}
left to right direction
hide empty description
state "Observe" as observe
state "EvaluateReady" as evaluate_ready
state "Ready" as ready
state "Retryable" as retryable
state "Failed" as failed
observe : read spec, tracked status, delete intent,\nand current OCI lifecycle
state "ResolveByLookup" as resolve_by_lookup
state "RejectUnsupportedDrift" as reject_unsupported_drift
state "ApplyUpdate" as apply_update
state "DeletePending" as delete_pending
state "Deleted" as deleted
state "DeleteCleanupBlocked" as delete_cleanup_blocked
[*] --> observe : CreateDistributedDatabase
observe --> resolve_by_lookup : tracked identity missing
resolve_by_lookup --> evaluate_ready : lookup or create reaches\nACTIVE, INACTIVE
resolve_by_lookup --> retryable : OCI state in CREATING,\nUPDATING, DELETING
resolve_by_lookup --> failed : unresolved OCI error or non-success state
observe --> evaluate_ready : OCI state in ACTIVE,\nINACTIVE
observe --> retryable : OCI state in CREATING,\nUPDATING, DELETING
observe --> failed : unresolved OCI error or non-success state
evaluate_ready --> reject_unsupported_drift : force-new or conflicting\ndrift detected
reject_unsupported_drift --> ready : wait for spec or live state change
evaluate_ready --> apply_update : supported mutable drift for\ndefinedTags, displayName,\nfreeformTags
apply_update --> ready : update path completes
evaluate_ready --> ready : no supported drift remains
ready --> ready : no supported drift remains
retryable --> retryable : OCI remains retryable
failed --> failed : OCI remains terminal
ready --> delete_pending : delete requested
retryable --> delete_pending : delete requested
failed --> delete_pending : delete requested
delete_pending --> delete_cleanup_blocked : cleanup or finalizer release remains blocked
delete_cleanup_blocked --> deleted : retry delete completion until allowed
deleted --> deleted : terminal stutter
note right of ready
shared diagram:
shared/diagrams/shared-controller-state-machine.svg
Start from the shared controller phase model and
specialize imported provider states, delete
targets, and failure exits here.
archetype batch: Generated service-manager
controllers map provider states into the shared
controller phases with explicit finalizer and
requeue policies.
service: distributeddatabase
slug: distributeddatabase
kind: DistributedDatabase
archetype: generated-service-manager
status/finalizer: required /
retain-until-confirmed-delete
requeue: provisioning, updating, terminating
provider states: create CREATING; update
UPDATING; delete DELETING
follow-up: create=read-after-write;
update=read-after-write; delete=confirm-delete
supported drift: definedTags, displayName,
freeformTags
reject before mutate: force-new fields
compartmentId
create-only fields:
catalogDetails.adminPassword,
catalogDetails.shardSpace,
shardDetails.adminPassword,
shardDetails.peerVmClusterIds
list lookup:
oci_globally_distributed_database_sharded_databases
filters compartmentId, displayName,
dbDeploymentType, lifecycleState; exact
compartmentId plus displayName list filters
preserve dbDeploymentType and lifecycleState
when already known, then narrow summary
candidates in memory to a unique exact prefix
plus dbDeploymentType match
conflicts: none
open gaps: none
Create-body normalization keeps shard and
catalog `source` inputs compatible with the OCI
SDK: CRD `EXISTING_CLUSTER` values serialize as
the SDK's `EXADB_XS`, scaffold-only `jsonData`
is dropped, and explicit false booleans in
nested vm-cluster and backup-config payloads are
preserved.
Reviewed lifecycle mapping treats CREATING as
provisioning, UPDATING as updating, ACTIVE and
INACTIVE as success, NEEDS_ATTENTION and FAILED
as terminal non-success, and DELETING as
terminating.
ListDistributedDatabases returns
DistributedDatabaseSummary items that omit
fields such as scanListenerPort,
latestGsmImageDetails, shardDetails,
catalogDetails, gsmDetails, dbBackupConfig, and
gsmSshPublicKey, so every successful bind or
write path rereads GetDistributedDatabase before
projecting steady-state status.
The provider resource exposes broader patch,
state-transition, and trigger update families,
but the current CRD does not publish those
controls; the package-local runtime only
performs in-place updates through
UpdateDistributedDatabaseDetails for
displayName, freeformTags, and definedTags.
Write-only shard and catalog passwords plus peer
VM cluster IDs are accepted during create but
omitted or projected through different OCI read
shapes; update parity ignores only those
unobservable inputs and still rejects drift in
observable shard or catalog fields.
Delete keeps the finalizer until
GetDistributedDatabase or list fallback confirms
DELETED or NOT_FOUND.
end note
note right of delete_pending
delete policy: required
delete observe: GetDistributedDatabase or
ListDistributedDatabases
delete targets: DELETED, NOT_FOUND
end note
@enduml
